# RFC 7950 Section 7.6.5: "Otherwise, if this ancestor is a case node, the leaf
# MUST exist if any node from the case exists in the data tree."
#
# remote/ip is mandatory in the tunnel-v4-endpoints grouping, and the closest
# ancestor of that leaf that is not a non-presence container is the gre case of
# the encapsulation kind choice (remote and gre are both non-presence
# containers). Writing `gre { ... }` makes the case exist, so remote ip is owed.
# Before the validator walked through choice and case entries, a gre tunnel with
# no remote endpoint passed `ze config validate`.
#
# VALIDATES: a gre tunnel with a local endpoint and no remote ip is refused, and
#            the refusal names the missing leaf, the rule, and the set command.
# PREVENTS: a tunnel with no remote endpoint reaching the backend, which builds
#           no unnumbered and no multipoint tunnel.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC7950-7.6.5-2 negative -- a gre case with local ip set and remote ip absent is refused by ze config validate, naming interface/tunnel[gre0]/encapsulation/gre/remote/ip as missing and the set command that adds it.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	tunnel gre0 {
		encapsulation {
			gre {
				local { ip 192.0.2.1; }
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=interface/tunnel[gre0]/encapsulation/gre/remote/ip
expect=stdout:contains=mandatory field "ip" is missing
expect=stdout:contains=set interface tunnel gre0 encapsulation gre remote ip <value>
